{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788376658,"nonce":"23hjgD3TOJV4y/h1TBiUcLvMw58=","title":"No verb installs a MinifiedThing, so anything the art bench makes can never be placed","message":"Found in play, run openrun-20260902 day 5.\n\n`Make_SculptureSmall` on a `TableSculpting` produces a **MinifiedThing**\n(`wooden small sculpture (normal)`, id 12500, sitting at [108,105]). Placing\nit needs an install blueprint. Nothing in the ~44-verb surface creates one:\n\n- `build {def:\"SculptureSmall\", ...}` is refused, correctly and informatively:\n  \"'SculptureSmall' is not BuildableByPlayer (Verse/BuildableDef: its\n  designationCategory is null, so no Designator_Build exists for it and it has\n  no blueprintDef either). It may still be spawnable — that is dev:spawn-thing.\"\n- `designate`'s type list has `uninstall` and no `install`\n  (cancel|chop|claim|cut|cut-plants|deconstruct|deconstruct-conduit|eject-fuel|\n  extract-skull|extract-tree|fill-in|harvest|harvest-wood|haul|hunt|mine|\n  mine-vein|open|release-to-wild|remove-floor|remove-foundation|slaughter|\n  smooth|smooth-floor|smooth-wall|strip|tame|uninstall)\n- `place-layout` takes defNames, not thing ids.\n\nSo the surface can UNINSTALL a building into a minified thing and can never put\none back. The mod already READS the other half — `ConstructionVerbs.cs:964`\nbranches on `Blueprint_Install` and explains that its material cost is empty —\nso the observation side is complete and only the act is missing.\n\n**This is a one-way ratchet, not just a gap.** Every craft at an art bench,\nand every uninstall, permanently increases a count that nothing can decrease.\n`checklists/daily.md`-adjacent guidance and the run contract both use\n`MinifiedThing == 0` as a health signal precisely because a nonzero count means\nfinished work is doing nothing — and on this verb surface that signal, once\ntripped, can never be cleared without `dev:*`, which is forbidden during play.\nIt also blocks the whole reinstall workflow (move a bench to a better room),\nwhich is the ordinary reason to uninstall in the first place.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A verb places an install blueprint for a MinifiedThing at a chosen cell —\n  whether that is `build {thing:\u003cminified id\u003e, at:P, rot:R}`, an\n  `install` designation type, or its own verb.\n- It reproduces the widget gate rather than the model: `GenConstruct`'s\n  `CanPlaceBlueprintAt` plus whatever `Designator_Install` checks, with the\n  same `{removal, reason}` blocker shape every other placement refusal uses,\n  and the interaction-cell clause reported the way `build` already reports it.\n- The result carries `placement_id` and journals an `action`, so an install\n  is auditable like any other placement, and `advance --until.layout` /\n  `construction` can watch it to completion.\n- Skill: an install blueprint is deliberately NOT skill-gated\n  (`ConstructionSkill.cs:333` already documents why), so `skill_shortfall`\n  must come back empty rather than absent.\n- Round-trip acceptance: `designate uninstall` a bench, then install it one\n  cell over, and `things --def MinifiedThing` returns to 0.","files":null}]}